{"id": "EUVD-2026-97714", "enisaUuid": "9eb6e145-657f-316c-a4ef-a1c4e65c0f95", "description": "ImageMagick before 7.1.2-32 contains a memory leak vulnerability in the -process option that allows attackers to cause unreleased memory allocations by supplying certain arguments. Attackers can repeatedly invoke the -process option with crafted arguments to gradually exhaust memory and degrade service availability.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T18:04:53", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-f32c-2v6j-wvh5", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/da4cfd78a2ceea4cf54207834f9d60c1b9c38797", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-before-7.1.2-32-memory-leak-via-process-option"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qrq6-phpr-492q", "CVE-2026-109270"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cc396c0b-940e-36d6-8574-221cd2cc73c9", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.0.0-0 <7.1.2-32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f1767f2c-9bbb-34ab-b660-7b7aa6c26d66", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}